concept:crimes-currency-act-1981-article-11 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "11 Counterfeit currency, as well as instruments or other articles referred to in"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:article-11 ;
    values:originalText "Article 3(5), should be seized and confiscated. Such currency, instruments or other articles should, after confiscation, be handed over on request either to the Government or bank of issue whose currency is in question, with the exception of exhibits whose preservation as a matter of record is required by the law of the country where the prosecution took place, and any specimens whose transmission to the Central Office mentioned in Article 12 may be deemed advisable. In any event, all such articles should be rendered incapable of use.   Schedule  International Convention for the Suppression of Counterfeiting Currency  Crimes (Currency) Act 1981  Compilation date: 11/5/18 Registered: 23/5/18" ;
    skos:definition "Article 3(5), should be seized and confiscated. Such currency, instruments or other articles should, after confiscation, be handed over on request either to the Government or bank of issue whose currency is in question, with the exception of exhibits whose preservation as a matter of record is required by the law of the country where the prosecution took place, and any specimens whose transmission to the Central Office mentioned in Article 12 may be deemed advisable. In any event, all such articles should be rendered incapable of use.   Schedule  International Convention for the Suppression of Counterfeiting Currency  Crimes (Currency) Act 1981  Compilation date: 11/5/18 Registered: 23/5/18"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "c25cc9d9648e039b76c64a44b28e092e92ea23d66687ff5956ee942e7a54825d" ;
    cof:pageNumber "31"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Counterfeit currency and instruments should be seized and confiscated." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
