concept:crimes-currency-act-1981-article-12 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "12 In every country, within the framework of its domestic law, investigations"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:article-12 ;
    values:originalText "on the subject of counterfeiting should be organised by a central office. This central office should be in close contact: (a) With the institutions issuing currency; (b) With the police authorities within the country; (c) With the central offices of other countries. It should centralise, in each country, all information of a nature to facilitate the investigation, prevention and punishment of counterfeiting currency." ;
    skos:definition "on the subject of counterfeiting should be organised by a central office. This central office should be in close contact: (a) With the institutions issuing currency; (b) With the police authorities within the country; (c) With the central offices of other countries. It should centralise, in each country, all information of a nature to facilitate the investigation, prevention and punishment of counterfeiting currency."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "e5d1152c188345b72c721fd8d5d4a5b0ad48d6b7a03d84c95462342c5102985c" ;
    cof:pageNumber "32"^^xsd:integer ;
